\newlabel{feasible}{{5}{6}{$ C $ is the cone generated by the active constraints at $ x^* $ and $ R $ is the feasible region for the LP problem. If $ x $ is in the cone given by the active constraints at $ x^* $ then $ \epsilon x $ is feasible for sufficiently small $ \epsilon > 0 $}{figure.5}{}}
